      "part_type": "Hadith",
      "path": "/books/al-kafi:3:4:8:4",
      "text": [
        " رَجُلٍ صَلَّى الْغَدَاةَ بِلَيْلٍ غَرَّهُ مِنْ ذَلِكَ الْقَمَرُ وَ نَامَ حَتَّى طَلَعَتِ الشَّمْسُ فَأُخْبِرَ أَنَّهُ صَلَّى بِلَيْلٍ قَالَ يُعِيدُ صَلَاتَهُ ."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.hubeali": [
          "And by this chain, from Fazalat, from Aban, from Zurara, ",
          "(It has been narrated) from Abu Ja’far<sup>asws</sup> regarding a man who prayed the morning <span class=\"iTxt\">Salāt</span> at night, the moon (light) having deceived him from that, and he slept until the emergence of the sun. So he was informed that he had prayed at night’. He<sup>asws</sup> said: ‘He should repeat his <span class=\"iTxt\">Salāt</span>’."
        ],
        "en.sarwar": [
          "4. Through the same chain of narrators as that of the previous Hadith it is narrated from Fadalah from Aban from Zurarah who has said the following: “Abu Ja‘far, ‘Alayhi al-Salam, about a man who performs the morning Salah (prayer) during the night mistakenly because of moon light and then goes to sleep until sunrise and he then is informed of having performed his morning Salah (prayer) during the night, has said, ‘He must perform it again.’” "
        ]
      }
    },
